WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.200
Financial firms run on data
and the vendors behind it.

2
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:08.710
Bloomberg, FactSet,
Morningstar, Smarsh, DocuSign,

3
00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:12.640
and contracts with long terms
and yearly price increases.

4
00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:16.340
Connexcy puts every contract
and invoice in one place,

5
00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:20.380
and pulls out the terms that matter:
renewal dates, notice periods,

6
00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:25.190
price increase caps and owners.
A person checks every one.

7
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.570
Your Bloomberg agreement renews for
two years, with 90 days' notice.

8
00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:32.783
Connexcy alerts your chief
operating officer six months out,

9
00:00:32.833 --> 00:00:35.287
while there's still room to negotiate.

10
00:00:35.597 --> 00:00:39.254
Every renewal is checked against its
contract. When Morningstar's quote is

11
00:00:39.304 --> 00:00:44.931
up 9% and your contract caps increases
at 5%, you'll know before you sign.

12
00:00:45.241 --> 00:00:49.058
And when an examiner asks why you
chose a vendor, the history is there:

13
00:00:49.108 --> 00:00:52.631
who approved it, everyone
involved, and their notes.

14
00:00:52.681 --> 00:00:57.161
Approvals run through operations,
compliance and the managing partner.

15
00:00:57.771 --> 00:01:01.614
Connexcy for financial
services. Every contract.

16
00:01:01.664 --> 00:01:06.464
Every invoice. Connected. Join
the beta at connexcy.com.
